## Rows skipped

a4 — Not applied. pcode=G0340028 is the Business Tax Act (營業稅法). English 004 labels that URL “Article 10 of the Value-Added and Non-Value-Added Business Tax Act”. The suggested title 各類所得扣繳率標準 is a different instrument. See reviewer-wrong.
a7 — Not applied. Adding (著作權) makes the Hindi services page annotate a Chinese term Vietnamese does not. guidance-disclosure-parity requires the same gloss set. Other locales are outside this lane.
a26 — Lakh/crore grouping. ACCEPTED-ROUND skip. Western commas kept (TWD 1,570,000 and the column figures). Pinned “TWD 1.57M” was not touched.
b12 — U+200B not deleted. Hindi 013 had 5 and 015 had 3, matching the Korean source. Removing them failed checkBlocks (013: 60 → 56, 015: 35 → 32) and the ZWSP count. Characters restored. The wording fixes in those files remain.
b16 — Heading ## 7 / ## 8 not renumbered. English and Korean have the same gap. Renumbering changes digits the checker counts.

## Systemic patterns and instance counts

- क्षेत्रीय / क्षेत्र read as a region when the English is an industry, a licence, or a type of business: 25. Left on purpose: भूमि उपयोग क्षेत्र (土地使用分區), अन्य क्षेत्र (another locality), treaty दूसरे क्षेत्र, 013 naming the area (Taipei City), 017 अनुमत क्षेत्र (Kinmen/Lienchiang operating area).
- परिणाम = 實績 / business performance, not a case outcome: 7. Outcome-परिणाम left.
- नियोजन read as planning when the English is employment: 3.
- “Center of life” calque: 3 (007 narrative, 007 checklist, 016 at death).
- Docket codes with a readable name plus the Chinese gloss: 3.
- विषय calquing 主體 / the responsible or legal person: 10, plus विज्ञापन की विषय-वस्तु (1). Topic-विषय (training subject, agenda, जाँच विषय) left. सूचीबद्धता का विषय left; that is “subject of a listing”, and the English is that a branch cannot be listed.
- आरोपण = vesting or who receives an estate asset: 11. दायित्व आरोपण, समाप्ति आरोपण, and tax/cost attribution left.
- U+200B deleted: 0 (8 restored).
- One-clause bank quotation repaired without merging blocks: 2 lines in 013.
- Gender: Wei Tseng stays feminine where Hindi marks it. 016 संरक्षकता now agrees (feminine). The male bank employee’s कहा stays masculine. अंतर्नियम agreement is grammatical gender of the noun, not her gender.

## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- a4: the shared URL is the Business Tax Act, not the non-resident dividend withholding schedule. The Hindi 001 label for that same URL already says “अनिवासियों को दिए गए लाभांश पर स्रोत कटौती दर”, which is what the review treated as the correct identification. English 001 calls it “General Business Tax Rate”. I did not copy the dividend label onto 004, and I did not rewrite the unflagged 001 label (that would be a new legal-title change, not this row).
- b16: the outline gap is in the English and the Korean. It is not a Hindi-only missing section.
- b12: the zero-width spaces are in the Korean source at the same counts. The checker will not allow them to be deleted.
- a26: Indian lakh grouping is what a native editor would write, and the review is right about that. ACCEPTED-ROUND forbids it because the checker does not parse it. Not applied.
- a14 suggested गारंटीकृत. That token is banned by the Hindi advertising scan even inside a disclaimer. The sentence now disclaims सुनिश्चित दृश्यता, which is the same proposition.
- a7 is a real missing gloss. It cannot be added in Hindi alone without failing gloss-set parity.

